-Function Requirement

Convert an integer `age` into a life period:

- If `age == 0`: return `INVALID`
- If `0 < age < 18`: return `CHILD`
- If `age >= 18`: return `ADULT`

- Boundary Test Cases

| Test Case | Input | Expected Output | Reason |
|-----------|--------|------------------|--------|
| TC1       | -1     | INVALID or Error | Negative input (invalid age) |
| TC2       | 0      | INVALID          | Lower boundary |
| TC3       | 1      | CHILD            | Just above INVALID |
| TC4       | 17     | CHILD            | Just below ADULT |
| TC5       | 18     | ADULT            | Exact boundary for ADULT |
| TC6       | 19     | ADULT            | Just above ADULT |
| TC7       | 100    | ADULT            | Large value input |
